Subject: [PATCH] bound an SDMA ring by the GART aperture at queue admission

Patch 0002 makes Gfx12GartTranslator::translate() pass an out-of-aperture
address through to local memory, which the driver needs: its indirect buffers
and its own page tables live in the frame buffer, outside the aperture. But
that also removed a check upstream states explicitly in
GpuDeviceSdma.RegisterBackedQueueRejectsAddressesOutsideTheGartAperture --
"an address outside it must fault rather than being reinterpreted as a
local-memory address" -- and that test is right.

Both are right because they are about different things. Measured against a real
amdgpu on gfx1250:

  SDMA ring                    0x6c00209000    inside  [0x6c00000000, 0x6c1fffffff]
  indirect buffer, page tables 0x68ec000       outside

The translator cannot tell a ring fetch from an IB fetch -- it is one level
below the distinction -- so enforcing ring bounds there also faults the IB and
deadlocks the driver. Enforce it at the layer that does know: refuse to arm a
register-backed SDMA queue whose ring does not lie wholly inside the published
aperture, and leave the translator permissive.

GpuVm gains gart_config() for this, recording the configuration publish_gart()
accepted and dropping it in clear_gart_binding(). With this, patch 0002 keeps
the driver working and the upstream test passes unmodified.

diff --git a/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp b/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
index 80022dbb75..e120aaa777 100644
--- a/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
+++ b/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
@@ -822,12 +822,18 @@ bool GpuVm::publish_gart(const GartConfig &config, std::shared_ptr<PhysicalMemor
   advance_access_state_locked(*binding);
   binding->translator = std::move(translator);
   binding->physical_memory = std::move(memory);
+  gart_config_ = config;
   ++binding->translation_epoch;
   if (binding->translation_epoch == 0)
     ++binding->translation_epoch;
   return true;
 }
 
+std::optional<GartConfig> GpuVm::gart_config() const {
+  std::lock_guard lock(mutex_);
+  return gart_config_;
+}
+
 bool GpuVm::clear_gart_binding() {
   std::lock_guard lock(mutex_);
   Binding *binding = find_locked(gart_address_space_);
@@ -838,6 +844,7 @@ bool GpuVm::clear_gart_binding() {
   binding->access_state = std::make_shared<GpuVmAccessState>();
   binding->translator.reset();
   binding->physical_memory.reset();
+  gart_config_.reset();
   ++binding->translation_epoch;
   if (binding->translation_epoch == 0)
     ++binding->translation_epoch;
